{
  "comment": [
    "The engine's pinned model manifest. Every checksum here is the authority:",
    "a file that does not hash to its pin is never written to the models dir.",
    "Embedded in the binary at compile time (include_str!), so it cannot be",
    "tampered with at runtime.",
    "",
    "Derived from spike/model-lock.json — the week-1 spike's measured record",
    "(ADR-0006, ADR-0008). Only the models v0.1 actually uses are listed; the",
    "spike also measured MobileCLIP2-S0 and CLIP ViT-B/32, both rejected, and",
    "they stay in the spike file as evidence rather than becoming pins here.",
    "",
    "Every checksum is read from the host, never computed from a file we",
    "happened to download. A pin taken from the local artefact certifies the",
    "local artefact, corruption included: the caption decoder below was pinned",
    "at 158331840 bytes for a file upstream had at 158599996, and the truncated",
    "copy passed its own checksum. `tests/models.rs` now audits every pin",
    "against what its host declares, and the size is what catches this.",
    "",
    "URLs name a commit rather than a branch. `resolve/main` is whatever `main`",
    "is today, so a pin against it goes stale the moment upstream commits to",
    "that file, and the install fails looking like the manifest is wrong.",
    "",
    "To change a pin: update the URL and checksum here AND in",
    "spike/model-lock.json, then let the engine re-embed that arm — a changed",
    "pin marks its vector space invalid rather than silently mixing vectors."
  ],
